-          "quote": "Let $q\\ge1$ be an integer. Let $Z_1,\\ldots,Z_q$ be mutually independent integrable real random variables on a common probability space, with means $m_j=\\mathbb E[Z_j]$, and suppose each is 1-sub-Gaussian, meaning that $\\mathbb E[\\exp(\\lambda(Z_j-m_j))]\\le\\exp(\\lambda^2/2)$ for every $\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$. Then for every $t\\ge0$,\n$$\n\\mathbb P\\!\\left(\\sum_{j=1}^q(Z_j-m_j)\\ge t\\right)\\le \\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{t^2}{2q}\\right),\\qquad\n\\mathbb P\\!\\left(\\sum_{j=1}^q(Z_j-m_j)\\le -t\\right)\\le \\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{t^2}{2q}\\right).\n$$",
